From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(instance): validate rejects invalid identifier shapes

### What
Pins validate_identifier via validate: empty or space-containing ids rejected, valid id accepted.

### Why it matters
Identifier validation is a fail-closed gate; weakening it admits malformed ids. Existing tests don't pin these shapes.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| validate_identifier -> Ok | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| empty check removed | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline: PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-instance --lib validate_rejects_bad_identifier`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
index d5f17444..119a0bd7 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
@@ -3120,4 +3120,15 @@ failure = "stop"
         c.memory_mib = 15;
         assert!(c.validate().is_err());
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn validate_rejects_bad_identifier() {
+        let mut c = InstanceConfig::parse(VALID.as_bytes()).unwrap();
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"bad id").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_err());
+        c.id = Text::from_bytes(b"demo").unwrap();
+        assert!(c.validate().is_ok());
+    }
 }
